author: pm-github
comments[10]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-28T05:25:22.563Z",codex-agent,Imported issue 303 with native provenance. Checking the duplicate attachment and status rejection against real non-git trackers and loopback GraphQL. Scope is Projects push and its receipt.
  "2026-11-28T05:25:54.447Z",codex-agent,"Reproduced 2 of 2 regressions on main 4fb4854 in non-git trackers. Two plans built from the empty board returned two draft IDs. A Status error after draft creation threw Sync wrote nothing; 1 operation(s) failed. Plan: serialize Projects push against complete live bindings, persist draft recovery before attachment, and expose per-step outcomes."
  "2026-11-28T05:32:34.328Z",codex-agent,The separate REST issue export component also submits two issue POST requests when applying two stale unlinked-item plans. Verified with an instrumented local transport. Tracked in GitHub issue 304 and its imported PM item. No REST export changes in this PR.
  "2026-11-28T05:43:00.596Z",codex-agent,"Projects push now rebuilds under the native ownership lease with a complete live board and tracker corpus, keeps a draft recovery record until its tag is confirmed, and returns independent attachment, Status and tag receipts. The initial 10 focused and 8 extended checks passed, including four packed npm and Bun format combinations. Running the cross-reference suite and behavioral reverts before push."
  "2026-11-28T06:08:46.489Z",codex-agent,The related suite exposed two fixtures that expected old Projects push behavior. Keep the missing attachment-ID assertion on a complete board and independently prove an ID-less board entry refuses before mutation. Assert stale tags are blocked and existing issue cards can backfill a tag without Status writes. Added the updated planner suite to the linked tests.
  "2026-11-28T06:14:27.656Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proofs in a disposable copy: seven isolated changes caused seven expected failures. Running the stale entry created two cards, dropping the absent-card and peer-claim guards lost their refusals, rethrowing the Status failure lost the accepted attachment receipt, discarding the retained card ID prevented recovery, restoring automatic 5xx retries replayed draft creation, and omitting pushReceipts broke the packed formatter check. The broad related run passed 1975 cases and flagged two old fixture expectations. Both corrected cases passed the targeted rerun, giving 1977 passing distinct cases across 68 related files."
  "2026-11-28T06:20:01.834Z",codex-agent,"The linked runner supplies an isolated PM_PATH. Two new fault-injection fixtures assumed implicit root discovery ignored it, so their recovery paths pointed at the runner's empty tracker. Their helpers now explicitly resolve the fixture tracker, matching the normal command path. Product code needed no change."
  "2026-11-28T06:28:19.138Z",codex-agent,"Final local verification: 1977 distinct related Node cases across 68 files, including the corrected fixture rerun. The three PM-linked commands passed 129 Node cases, 40 native Bun cases, and 175 planner and ownership cases. Packed npm and Bun launchers passed all four JSON and TOON combinations. Typecheck, both builds, lint, docstrings (344 declarations), duplication (37 modules and zero duplicated lines), and the ownership inventory (106 groups and 336 sites) passed. The related REST export defect is in issue 304. Full release and coverage gates are left to CI."
  "2026-11-28T06:36:55.468Z",codex-agent,"Exact head 1b115ee passed CodeQL and Semgrep. Two Projects push review findings reproduced or verified against the change: discussion r4725852740 raced a native issue claim through the tag write and observed one unwanted Status mutation; r4725852746 identified ambiguous delivery wording that implied certainty. The candidate rereads complete tracker authority for the confirmed card before Status and reports that it could not confirm any writes after unknown delivery. Re-running related gates before delivery."
  "2026-11-28T06:47:13.942Z",codex-agent,"Review regression evidence: the original 1b115ee Status path sent one mutation after a concurrent native issue claim. With the pre-Status rerender it sent zero, reported a partial result, and retained the written tag. The unknown-delivery fixture previously emitted Sync confirmed no writes and now requires Sync could not confirm any writes. Both new focused checks passed. Typecheck, builds, lint, docstrings, ownership inventory and zero-duplication checks passed for the follow-up. The related suite is rerunning before push."
